        { q: 'Find $n$ given that $\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^3 = 4356$.', solution: ['Take the Nicomachus read: $\\sum r^3 = \\left[\\tfrac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right]^2$, so $\\tfrac{n(n+1)}{2} = \\sqrt{4356} = 66$.', 'Now, solve the triangular equation: $n(n+1) = 132$ — try $n = 11$: $11 \\cdot 12 = 132$ exactly.', 'So, $n = 11$ — and monotonicity of the triangular numbers makes it the unique seat.', 'Hence $n = 11$: the sum of cubes to eleven is $66^2 = 4356$.'], answer: 'n = 11' },
